/-! # The four collision parents' satisfaction theorems from DATA ONLY (round par/satc2)

`<p>_satC` (`MemNameCollisionSatCertTest`) applied `Tools.ShippingSatCert.satOfCert` to the head
conclusion `<p>_designClosedBW hr entry hR0`, and `<p>_designClosedBW` was generated by
`generateTopW` from the hand-written run lemmas (`<p>_runFacts`, `<p>_outsG0`, `<p>_typedRun`,
`<p>_designP0`, `<p>_names`). Here:

* `<p>_designClosedCW` — `Tools.ShippingSatCert2Command.generateCert2WTop` (the data route of
  `generateCert2` with the wiring-exporting head `machine_design_noPortsTBW`); its statement is
  asserted `Expr`-equal to `<p>_designClosedBW`'s.
* `<p>_satC2` — ONE application of `satOfCert` to `<p>_designClosedCW hr entry hR0`; its statement
  is asserted `Expr`-equal to `<p>_sat`'s.

Per parent the inputs are ONLY: the certificate `<p>_cert` (`gateParentCertOk`, one `decide`,
`MemNameCollisionGateCertGenTest`), `memGateOk` (kernel `Eq.refl true` in the generator, `decide`
in `satOfCert`'s argument), `satDataOk` (`decide`), the parent's reader facts `machine_ok` /
`machine_body`, the gate source's `gate_old` / `gate_peel` / `gate_wf`, the tables `outsG` /
`insG` (`outsFN` / `insFN`), the memory origin `cb 4 8`, the closing `<p>_closesR`, the value
equation (`syncGate_value` / `comboGate_value`), and the outer premises `hr`, `entry`, `hR0`, `hB`.
Generator-produced endpoints (`f.machine_ships_hierRG`, `f.machine_composedTRGA(W)`) are used as
the generators made them.

SCOPE: `memGateOk` covers parents with a single gate child and a single memory origin, data
(gate result) width ≠ 1; the certificate does NOT cover all compiler-accepted inputs; `hinit`
(slot inits `0`) remains a restriction of `sat_of_designClosedBW`; only the memory-free one-level
composed route (`composedG_of_T`, `Reset1`) is handled by the generator.

The audit asserts per parent: both statements `Expr`-equal as above; standard axioms; neither
proof (`<p>_designClosedCW`'s, `<p>_satC2`'s) mentions `<p>_designClosedBW`, `<p>_designClosedB`,
or any hand-written run/kid lemma (`_runFacts`, `_outsG0`, `_designP0`, `_typedRun`, `_names`,
`_gate`, `_oi`, `_inputWires`, `_kidsSat`, `_kidNoRegs`, `_kids`, `_kidTyped`, `_entry`,
`_outChars`, `_callWidths`, `_callArgs`, `fakeSrc_width`, `fakeN_width`) in any of the test
namespaces; `<p>_satC2` uses `satOfCert` and `<p>_designClosedCW`; `<p>_designClosedCW` uses
`memGate_kidsS`, `memGate_kidTypedS`, the five `gateParent_*` and `machine_design_noPortsTBW`.

GLOBAL NAMES added: `Sparkle.Tests.Compiler.MemNameCollisionSatCert2Test.<p>_designClosedCW` and
`.<p>_satC2` (new namespace). -/

